{# ===========================================================================
   Component: menu-links

   Two links under a location page's dish list: the full menu, and this room's
   printable menu.

   USAGE
     {% set menuLinksLoc = loc.id %}
     {% include "components/menu-links.njk" %}

   OUTLINED, NOT RED. The header CTA is red and spends the page's one red
   under DESIGN_SYSTEM.md's rule of a single primary CTA per viewport. These
   are secondary routes to a document, so they take the hairline-outlined
   treatment the phone buttons on /happy-hour/ already use.

   THE FILE TYPE AND SIZE ARE ON THE LINK, and that is an accessibility
   requirement rather than a nicety: a link that silently starts a 785KB
   download on cellular is a link that lied about what it does. The type also
   warns that this leaves the page for a document. Plaza Bonita's is a JPG,
   not a PDF, and says so.

   A room with no file in locationMenus.json renders only the /menu/ link.
   That is Maui, which was not in the supplied set. It gets no printable link
   rather than a broken one, and certainly not a San Diego menu standing in
   for a room that runs its own menu at its own prices.

   No `download` attribute. These open in the browser's viewer, which is what
   someone checking a menu on a phone wants; forcing a save is worse for the
   common case and browsers already offer the save.
   =========================================================================== #}
{%- set roomMenu = locationMenus[menuLinksLoc] %}
<p class="menu-links">
  <a class="menu-links__link" href="/menu/">View full menu</a>
  {%- if roomMenu %}
  <a class="menu-links__link" href="{{ roomMenu.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
    Printable menu
    <span class="menu-links__meta">{{ roomMenu.typeLabel }}, {{ roomMenu.sizeLabel }}</span>
    <span class="u-visually-hidden">, opens in a new tab</span>
  </a>
  {%- endif %}
</p>
